{"id":"68e08385-71b7-491a-aacf-19628e472d13","revision":0,"last_node_id":36,"last_link_id":45,"nodes":[{"id":1,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[0,-460],"size":[4300,400],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Arbor · Orbit — every character in every place · FastH3 OmniRef (MiniMax H3, 8 steps)\n\nOne **Load Media** holds everything: a group per character (`# Mei`, `# Kai`) and one group with the places. Every character goes into every place, and the camera makes a full 360° orbit around them — six clips, filed **one branch per character**.\n\n1. **Load Media** → its *files* output is the data tree: `{0} Mei`, `{1} Kai`, `{2} Places`. Two **Tree Branch** nodes take it apart by name: *Mei, Kai* and *Places*.\n2. **Cross Reference** pairs every character with every place: `{0} Mei` gets the three places, `{1} Kai` gets the three places. The **Panel** on its output shows the pairs as thumbnails.\n3. **Prompt Template** (*zip*) writes one structured OmniRef prompt per clip: the **Who** panel has one branch per character (`{name}` is the branch's name), the **Sound** panel one line per place, and the shorter list repeats — the same pairing, in text.\n4. **Tree to Data** lines the pictures up for **MiniMax H3 Reference to Video**: the character is `<Picture 1>`, the place `<Picture 2>`. The **Length** panel types a number (frames, 17k + 5) straight into the node.\n5. **Construct Tree** with the pairs as its *shape* puts the clips back into `Mei` / `Kai`: **Video Grid** plays characters × places, **Save by Path** files them, and the **Compare Viewer**'s branch chip shows one character at a time — flip or wipe between the places.\n\n0.98 MP (1344 × 768), 158 frames (~6.6 s) per clip, about 3–4 min each on a 16 GB card. Add characters or places with **Add…** on Load Media — the pairs, prompts and grid follow."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Arbor · Orbit — every character in every place · FastH3 OmniRef (MiniMax H3, 8 steps)\n\nOne **Load Media** holds everything: a group per character (`# Mei`, `# Kai`) and one group with the places. Every character goes into every place, and the camera makes a full 360° orbit around them — six clips, filed **one branch per character**.\n\n1. **Load Media** → its *files* output is the data tree: `{0} Mei`, `{1} Kai`, `{2} Places`. Two **Tree Branch** nodes take it apart by name: *Mei, Kai* and *Places*.\n2. **Cross Reference** pairs every character with every place: `{0} Mei` gets the three places, `{1} Kai` gets the three places. The **Panel** on its output shows the pairs as thumbnails.\n3. **Prompt Template** (*zip*) writes one structured OmniRef prompt per clip: the **Who** panel has one branch per character (`{name}` is the branch's name), the **Sound** panel one line per place, and the shorter list repeats — the same pairing, in text.\n4. **Tree to Data** lines the pictures up for **MiniMax H3 Reference to Video**: the character is `<Picture 1>`, the place `<Picture 2>`. The **Length** panel types a number (frames, 17k + 5) straight into the node.\n5. **Construct Tree** with the pairs as its *shape* puts the clips back into `Mei` / `Kai`: **Video Grid** plays characters × places, **Save by Path** files them, and the **Compare Viewer**'s branch chip shows one character at a time — flip or wipe between the places.\n\n0.98 MP (1344 × 768), 158 frames (~6.6 s) per clip, about 3–4 min each on a 16 GB card. Add characters or places with **Add…** on Load Media — the pairs, prompts and grid follow."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":2,"type":"Arbor_LoadMedia","pos":[0,0],"size":[420,640],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"files","name":"files","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"files"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"files","name":"files","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":[1,2]},{"localized_name":"names","name":"names","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":null},{"localized_name":"images","name":"images","shape":6,"type":"IMA